    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This podcast explores the ways that sounds affect us. It focuses on water as a case study and provides research for why certain sounds are more calming than others. The categories discussed are broken up into repetitive sounds, white noise, and sounds that come from nature. The podcast is initiated with three stories of people whose lives have been impacted by the sound of water. These people are Mina Shah, Will Robins, and Caitlin Hird, whom I thank greatly for participating in this podcast.",
